:0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nGodot v4.6.dev4\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - integrated Intel(R) Iris(R) Xe Graphics (Intel Corporation; 32.0.101.7076) - 11th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-1135G7 @ 2.40GHz (8 threads) - 15.80 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen starting the game for the first time after launching the editor, the engine prints an error for every script that does not have a `class_name` assigned\nERROR: Cannot get class 'script_name.gd'.\n\n<img width=\"914\" height=\"349\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/021b8a78-8e07-4bb0-b498-de080d27f26f\" />\n\n<img width=\"601\" height=\"144\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9cf30814-b801-4880-9595-255abea47723\" />\n\nI found this line in the `EditorNode::_get_class_or_script_icon`:\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/b15a13eed39d902fafb14ca0637c5827c80b2bc9/editor/editor_node.cpp#L5513\nBoth `ClassDB::is_virtual` and `ClassDB::can_instantiate` throw errors\n\nI haven’t found any negative consequences from this behavior. Everything works normally. But the messages still clutter the output, especially in projects with many unnamed scripts\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a new scene\n2. Attach a new script\n3. Leave the `class_name` field empty\n4. Run the scene - observe the error\n\n(Optional) Go to Project > Reload Current Project to invalidate the icon cache. Run the scene again - the error appears again\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[cannot-get-class-bug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23625961/cannot-get-class-bug.zip)\n\nJust run the game","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":